---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro'
import DocsShell, { GUIDE } from '../../../components/DocsShell.astro'
import PlayCell from '../../../components/PlayCell.astro'
import Code from '../../../components/Code.astro'

const page = GUIDE.find((p) => p.slug === 'relationships')!

const EAGER = `@NodeEntity()
export class Movie {
  @Property({ type: 'string', unique: true, primary: true })
  title: string

  @OneToMany(() => Person, 'ACTED_IN', { direction: 'out', eager: true })
  actors: Person[]
}

const movie = await neode.find(Movie, title, { with: { actors: true } })`

const CARDINALITY = `@NodeEntity()
export class Person {
  @Uuid({ primary: true })
  id: string

  @OneToOne({
    type: 'LIVES_AT',
    target: () => Address,
    direction: 'out',
    cardinality: 'one',          // at most one edge — a second relate() throws
    enforce: 'currentOccupantId', // @Unique property on Address
    claimConflict: 'throw',       // 'refuse' (default) | 'detach' | 'throw'
  })
  address: Address | undefined
}`

const toc = [
  { href: '#eager', label: 'Eager loading' },
  { href: '#cardinality', label: 'Cardinality & claims' },
  { href: '#edges', label: 'Relationship entities' },
  { href: '#read-models', label: 'Read models' },
  { href: '#try', label: 'See it' },
]
---

<Base title="neode — Relationships">
  <DocsShell current="relationships" toc={toc} prev={{ href: 'models', label: 'Defining models' }} next={{ href: 'traversals', label: 'Traversals' }}>
    <h1 style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,44px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em">{page.title}</h1>
    <p class="txt" style="font-size:18px">
      <code>@OneToOne</code> and <code>@OneToMany</code> describe edges from a model. Mark one eager and neode loads it in
      the same statement as the node.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec" id="eager">Eager loading</h2>
    <p class="txt">Ask for the relationship via the <code>with</code> option and the whole thing comes back hydrated, in one Cypher statement.</p>
    <Code code={EAGER} />

    <h2 class="sec" id="cardinality">Cardinality &amp; claims</h2>
    <p class="txt">
      <code>cardinality</code> is a write-time guard: <code>'one'</code> / <code>'zeroOrOne'</code> relationships hold at
      most one edge per node — a second <code>relate()</code> throws <code>CardinalityViolationError</code>. Swap an edge
      with <code>syncEdges()</code> or <code>replaceRelationship()</code>; both detach first.
    </p>
    <p class="txt">
      <code>enforce</code> turns the <em>inverse</em> side into a database-level guarantee. It names a
      <code>@Unique</code> property on the target model, and every write path keeps it pointed at the source node's
      primary key — the target's uniqueness constraint then rejects a second node claiming it, raw Cypher included.
      <code>replaceRelationship()</code> and <code>syncEdges()</code> move the claim atomically, and
      <code>delete()</code> releases it. <code>claimConflict</code> picks what <code>relate()</code> does when the target
      is already claimed by a different source: <code>'refuse'</code> (default — resolves <code>undefined</code>),
      <code>'detach'</code> (the claim moves) or <code>'throw'</code>.
    </p>
    <Code code={CARDINALITY} />
    <p class="txt">
      The forward side (one target per source) stays an application-level guard: Neo4j has no edge-count constraint, so
      serialize writers when it must hold under concurrency.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec" id="edges">Relationship entities</h2>
    <p class="txt">
      When an edge carries properties, model it as an entity with <code>@StartNode</code> and <code>@EndNode</code>. Create
      and remove edges with <code>relate()</code> and <code>detach()</code>, and use cascade deletes when a node should take
      its edges with it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec" id="read-models">Read models</h2>
    <p class="txt">Read-model decorators describe what a read should return. All of them are projected into one query per read, so there is no N+1.</p>
    <dl style="margin:0 0 8px">
      <div class="dl"><dt>@RelatedOne</dt><dd>A single related node</dd></div>
      <div class="dl"><dt>@RelatedMany</dt><dd>A list of related nodes</dd></div>
      <div class="dl"><dt>@RelationshipCount</dt><dd>How many edges, without loading them</dd></div>
      <div class="dl"><dt>@RelationshipExists</dt><dd>Whether an edge exists</dd></div>
      <div class="dl"><dt>@Computed, @Expression</dt><dd>Derived values computed in the same statement</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <h2 class="sec" id="try">See it</h2>
    <PlayCell recipe="relationships" />
  </DocsShell>
</Base>
